        "dict-easton",
        "Dictionary",
        "Easton.",
        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>NAUGHTY FIGS</strong> (Jeremiah 24:2). “The bad figs may have been such either from having decayed, and thus been reduced to a rotten condition, or as being the fruit of the sycamore, which contains a bitter juice” (Tristram, Nat. Hist.). The inferiority of the fruit is here referred to as an emblem of the rejected Zedekiah and his people.",
